  The tail you want already ships with Eve. This demo never attaches to it, so the page is watching a log the\
  pipeline writes by hand.\
\
  Why the activity feed is quiet\
\
  The review page does not talk to Eve. harness serve starts executeRun in the Node process and the UI tails\
  runs/<id>/trace.jsonl.\
\
  Eve is a second front door. Its only tool awaits that same function and returns when the whole review is\
  done:\
\
   agent/tools/run_pipeline.ts lines 8-16\
\
  export default defineTool(\{\
    description: "Run the impact harness for one monitored-authority scenario. Returns the run id, status,\
  and output directory.",\
    // ...\
    async execute(input) \{\
      // ...\
      const trace = await executeRun(\{ repo, runDir, scenario, config, mode: \{ kind: "full" \} \});\
      return \{ run_id: trace.run_id, status: trace.status, out: runDir \};\
    \},\
  \});\
\
  Inside that call, the orchestrator and stack analysts use generateText. That call returns only after the\
  step finishes. The events you render are the ones runAgent emits itself: tool start, tool finish, and a\
  "still working" heartbeat every 5 seconds. Reasoning tokens and partial text never leave the provider call.\
\
  eve dev would show one long run_pipeline invocation and then a result. Agent Runs on Vercel would show the\
  same shape. The Claude Code-style transcript is bound to Eve actions (tool calls, reasoning deltas,\
  subagent sessions), and this review is not an Eve action. It is a function body.\
\
  What is already there, with no viewer to build\
\
  Eve's terminal UI is the closest thing to Claude Code, Codex, or the Cursor CLI. eve dev --tools full\
  --reasoning collapsed --subagents full streams the turn in the terminal: tool arguments, results,\
  reasoning, and subagent sections. /traces opens a live viewer over .eve/traces/v1. eve dev\
  https://your-deployment attaches that same UI to a deployed agent. This only becomes a useful demo after\
  the review's steps are Eve tools or subagents, not one opaque tool.\
\
  useEveAgent() from eve/react is the browser version of that stream. It resumes a durable session (resume:\
  true replays history and follows an in-flight turn after refresh), and it projects assistant text,\
  reasoning, and tool parts as they arrive. eve add channel/web generates a Next.js chat that already renders\
  tool results, errors, and approval prompts. A delegated analyst is its own session: the parent emits\
  subagent.called, and the client follows the child with session.streamSubagent() (current docs also show\
  agent() plus stream()). You do not write a jsonl tail. You do render parts.\
\
  Agent Runs is the hosted inspector: sessions, turns, tools, reasoning, timing, tokens, with no\
  instrumentation file. It is a dashboard, not the product page. Fine for you during the review; weak if the\
  demo is the product.\
\
  Eve's own session stream is NDJSON (message.appended, reasoning.appended, action.input.appended,\
  actions.requested, action.result, subagent.called). The hand-rolled /api/runs/:id/trace endpoint is a\
  second protocol for events Eve would have emitted if it had been allowed to see them.\
\
  What moving the job onto the AI SDK and AI Elements would drop\
\
  The model loop is already the AI SDK. src/models.ts calls generateText from ai. AI Elements does not\
  observe anything. It is a shadcn registry: React 19 components, Tailwind 4, copied into the repo. The\
  zero-mapping path is useChat plus streamText().toUIMessageStreamResponse(), which assumes a chat\
  transcript. This page is a job that ends in a ranked report. The registry also assumes a Next.js app. This\
  UI is a Vite bundle served by the harness, with no Tailwind.\
\
  Dropping Eve and driving the review through useChat would give you the component look, and you would give\
  up:\
\
  \'95 A session that survives the tab closing, a cold start, and a redeploy. Today the "background" behavior\
    is void executeRun(...) in src/server.ts. If that process dies, the run dies. Eve's Workflow log is the\
    piece that actually keeps going.\
  \'95 The terminal tail, /traces, and Agent Runs.\
  \'95 Child sessions for parallel stack analysts, including following them from the parent.\
  \'95 Park-and-resume for approvals, schedules, sandbox, and other channels.\
  \'95 The chatgpt() model pin from eve/models/openai, which this repo uses for gpt-5.6-luna.\
\
  WorkflowAgent (@ai-sdk/workflow) is the AI SDK's durable loop, and it is a rebuild of that shell. It has no\
  generate(), no TUI, and no Agent Runs. Its tool-input callbacks are recorded during the model step and\
  replayed after the step completes, so a live token tail is still a stream you plumb to the client. You\
  would also still own the report page.\
\
  A third option, Langfuse or Braintrust via OpenTelemetry, is another developer dashboard. Eve already\
  exports those spans. It does not make the demo.\
\
  What I would do\
\
  Keep executeRun as the eval and CLI path. The stage machine, citation checks, ranking, and fault injection\
  are the judgment. Turning that into a freeform chat agent so the stream looks busy would throw away the\
  part worth defending.\
\
  For the demo, split the Eve tool into the steps a person can watch: diff, company gate, scope, one subagent\
  per stack, rank. Each of those is a real Eve action, so eve dev --tools full and useEveAgent tail them\
  with no jsonl format of your own. Point the review page at the session and resume it. Closing the tab and\
  coming back to a still-moving review is the background behavior this harness was chosen for, and it is the\
  one the current poll loop only approximates.\
\
  If that is more surface area than you want this week, stay on the Vite page and switch the inner\
  generateText to streamText, writing fullStream deltas into the existing tail. That makes this page show\
  reads, reasoning, and partial text. It stays your event schema, and Eve's TUI still will not see inside\
  run_pipeline.\
\
  I would not restyle this app onto AI Elements just for the chrome. Tool, Reasoning, and ChainOfThought are\
  presentational; you would still map events onto props, and you would take on Tailwind and shadcn to do it.\
  Use them if you want that visual language on a Next page that is already an Eve or useChat session. They\
  are not an observability layer.\
\
